WEBVTT

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.700
We're almost there, Takayama.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.870
Geez.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.450
Takayama!

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.040
Oh dear.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.390
If you don't wake up, you're gonna get left behind, sleepyhead.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.350
Thank you for riding with us.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.430
We will soon be arriving at our final stop, Aomori.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.220
Crap!
We will soon be arriving at our final stop, Aomori.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.100
We will soon be arriving at our final stop, Aomori.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.350
We will be pulling in to platform 3. The doors will open on the left.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.080
Aomori.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.910
Aomori.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.410
Thank you again for riding with us.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.040
This is our last stop, Aomori.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.170
Okay!

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.460
Is something funny?

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.300
It's just like you. I think it's cute.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.100
There you go.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.370
Sorry again for making you
help me sort things out.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.250
And for having you write all those apologies.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.880
It's part of the job. I'm your deputy, after all.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.000
Not to mention,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.470
I really made a mess for you and Captain Gonou the other day with the Hokutosei incident.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.260
I'm the one who told you to go ahead and take action if you think you're right.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.640
Taking responsibility for these things is <i>my</i> job as squad captain.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.190
Oh?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.720
Looks like it's in.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.690
That sounds like...

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.370
The JNR KiHa381!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.760
I'm glad you seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.180
A hood like that is really rare.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.850
Some say it looks like a dog face, so they call it the bulldog.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.270
I love it, though!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.020
I could do without the noise, though!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:23.740
That's a 12,000 horsepower gas turbine engine in there. It's based off a helicopter one.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:29.330
Thanks to that, it's the fastest diesel train of all the JNR express lines.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.080
Oh, no one else is here.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.590
Ms. Iida, take the window view.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.920
Thank you.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.470
I should be thanking you.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.180
I get to ride on a KiHa381!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.810
It's only used for special occasions.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.230
Special occasions?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:05:02.070
You know how close to New Year's the trains get super packed, so special trains are put to work?

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.360
Hey, yeah.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.990
Apparently the original plan was to use newer express trains.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:11.160
But they had to be pulled at the last minute because of problems,

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.370
and suddenly it was the
older models' time to shine.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.670
The Express Hatsukari bound for Tokyo will now be leaving platform 2.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.810
Thank you for riding on the Express Hatsukari.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:42.440
We will be stopping at Asamushi Onsen, Noheji, Misawa, Hachinohe,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:53.830
Sannohe, Morioka, Hanamaki, Ichinoseki, Sendai, Fukushima, Koriyama, Utsunomiya,

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.580
Omiya, and Ueno.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:01.590
We are estimated to arrive at our final stop, Tokyo, at 7:30 p.m.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.520
Ms. Iida, that sound.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.560
What?

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.520
I didn't hear anything.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.520
I know I heard it!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.070
Let's leave it to the staff onboard.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.650
We're just taking the train home to Tokyo.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.660
Sorry, it's really bothering me!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.740
Hey!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.710
You're pretty early today, Haruka.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.590
I could say the same about you, Aoi.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.670
N-Not really.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.180
Well, well. You certainly are early.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.010
So are you, Captain Gonou.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.560
I got a call from Nana.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.810
Did something happen to Takayama?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.310
He's in trouble again, isn't he?

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.940
Is that why you're early?
You were worried?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.110
N-No, not really...

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.190
What is it this time?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:11.360
Why does he attract danger
wherever he goes?

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.080
I'd worry less about him and more about yourselves, girls.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.370
It's very dangerous beyond this point.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.790
Please, stay out.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.920
I heard a strange sound.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.840
I think something might have gone wrong.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.470
Wh-Who are you?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.720
A trainee in the Student Railway OJT program.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.640
A student?

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.110
Um...

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.700
This sound must mean there's
something wrong, don't you think?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.450
I love the KiHa381.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.420
I've listened to my friend's recordings of its sounds a million times.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.420
But I've never heard it make this sound.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.670
It's like it's crying for help.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.800
I've been driving this baby
ever since I joined JNR.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.590
We've been through some
tough times together.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.970
I'm not about to take an outsider's opinion.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.810
It's just his pride.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.690
This is his last drive, after all.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.830
Figure anything out?

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.790
No.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.960
At least you tried.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.590
I can still do something.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.670
Wait, wait, wait!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.880
Oh, good morning, Takayama.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.640
Why're you calling so early?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:58.970
Huh?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.140
Listen to a gas turbine engine?

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.640
Well? Can you tell anything?

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.560
Even I couldn't hear anything from that.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.270
All right. Sorry to bug you
so early in the morning.

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:11.690
Thanks, Sasshou!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.240
Hey, wait!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.780
Geez.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:15.910
What was that about?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.320
Huh?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.910
The KiHa381 engine manual?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.290
Yeah, okay. I'll check.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.370
I'll call you if I find anything.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.080
Takayama!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.420
Why is Haruka the first person you call?

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:35.880
It's like he's lumping me
with Iwaizumi or something!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.590
'Sup? You say my name?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.760
Just forget it, Walter White.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:44.230
Man, Takayama is just totally
butting in on this thing.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.810
We have jurisdictions for a reason.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.400
He should just chill out.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.980
It's just like him to care, though.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.650
Aoi, can you look at this?

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.900
Sure, sure.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.120
O-Ow, hot!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.700
Are you okay?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.250
I saw my life flash before my eyes!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.370
Let me see.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.630
Ms. Iida?

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:16.340
I asked Koumi to look into it, and she said
it might be the cooling fan belt wearing out.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.050
That doesn't mean you should try to work on a running engine.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.810
It's super dangerous!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:23.930
I'm sorry.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.690
Besides, not just anyone
can change out a belt.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.690
And of course, I would have left <i>that</i> to the professionals.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.650
Are you hearing me?

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:37.190
But it's okay for me to help by
looking for a replacement, right?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.450
Let's see.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.830
A thin piece of cloth with elasticity.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.160
Elasticity, huh?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.790
Huh?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.300
Maybe...

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.300
Huh?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.150
You really think this will work?

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.480
I asked Koumi to check.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.610
She said it's possible
it'd last till we get to Tokyo.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.860
Here.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.240
But no staring.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.010
That face says it worked out.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:40.510
Yeah.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:44.470
The driver even said she's
running smoother now.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.600
That's good.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.640
That's a rail bus!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.390
Yup.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.810
Adorable.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:24.390
When the KiHa381 was still in regular service, this was a bustling shop.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.260
Sasshou, was it?

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.850
There were girls here that wore cute uniforms just like hers.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.600
It really was lively.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:37.820
Makes you wish this train
would keep running forever.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.160
She's finally starting to show her stuff.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:59.090
This tilting train body was designed to make taking curbs possible at high speeds and more comfortable.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:05.510
JNR developed the KiHa381 as a pendulum-type
gas turbine-powered locomotive by taking into account

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.890
the successes of the French high-speed trains, after all.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:17.100
Boy, it's pretty hot in here.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.370
Something's not right.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:30.530
H-Huh?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.420
It's not working.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.930
A service power failure?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.930
The KiHa381 is a diesel locomotive, right?

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:57.690
So it takes its power not from overhead lines but from the diesel generator.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:02.230
Apparently the service power getting cut on the air conditioning

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:08.700
is one chronic problem it's inherited from its prototype, the KiHa80 series.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.700
You again?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.330
I just want to check something. I'll be out of your hair soon.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:18.120
The air conditioning's breaker is down.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.420
Why?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.880
Maybe you can just hold it up
until we get to Tokyo.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.760
Please don't joke like that.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.760
Good timing, then.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:36.100
This might come in handy.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.310
Our chopsticks for lunch?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.310
You knew this would happen?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:45.780
Trouble sure seems to love you, Takayama.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.860
What was that?

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:50.450
I said, maybe the goddess of trouble has a thing for you!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.200
Ah-choo!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.620
Are you okay, Aoi?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.790
It's Takayama!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.250
I bet he's talking smack about me!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.760
I hope things worked out for him.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.470
Takayama, hold up.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.220
What was that?

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.570
It sounded like something just shorted out.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:25.270
Yeah.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.780
And the air conditioning's still offline.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.700
If we can just figure out why...

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.530
I wish we could do something.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.540
If this keeps up, it'll be like we're in a sauna with our clothes on.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.540
Talk about gross.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:43.540
It might be good for losing a few pounds, but I'm not worried about my weight.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.010
Huh? Again?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.760
Now what?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.140
Ms. Iida!

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.440
Figure something out?

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.770
Koumi really hit the books hard.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.520
There are a few things we can try.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.780
You go take a break.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.490
You're pouring sweat.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.610
Too late for that.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.200
I'm seeing this through to the end.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.210
Looks like we're in the clear.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.090
Thank goodness.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.420
I couldn't have done it
without you, Ms. Iida.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:36.050
I would have been screwed on my own.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.890
Well, I was just gonna ignore it, originally.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.020
But you wouldn't let me.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.390
You just don't play fair.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:46.270
I couldn't stand to just sit and watch you dash headlong into danger.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:50.360
I guess I did it on instinct.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.820
Reminds me of Hitomi.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:53.360
Ah-choo!
Reminds me of Hitomi.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.660
Must be Nana talking about me.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.620
Honestly, what is she doing?

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.620
Thank you very much for your help today.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.670
And I'm sorry for being such a busybody.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.420
Is the driver mad?

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.460
Oh, he's always like that.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.510
Thank you ever so much.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:15.630
No problem.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.430
Sorry about that!

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.770
Enjoy your ride, now.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.310
I know we're almost to Tokyo, but still.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:28.980
Head Conductor!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.320
What is it?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.320
What's up, Takayama?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:37.200
It's nothing. I'll be right back.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.910
Hey!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:40.830
Geez.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:45.040
There's no way it's nothing if you're running.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.040
Everyone's waiting, Deputy.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.360
Tokyo.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.370
We're back!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.240
I guess everyone went home already.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:29.330
Wanted to thank Sakurai
and Koumi for today, huh?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.340
I can do it tomorrow.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.800
And you forgot Iwaizumi, Ms. Iida.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.010
The four of us are K4.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:39.760
The five of us, you mean.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.180
Don't forget me, now.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.640
Sorry about that.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.640
Are you really?

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.980
You totally forgot about me, didn't you?

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.150
Of course not!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.400
Good work out there today.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:03.410
Hitomi told me she gave everyone the day off tomorrow.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.000
After the Hokutosei incident,
you could use the break.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.920
Rest up and recharge.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.210
I'll see you next week, Takayama.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.050
Huh.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:21.430
With tomorrow off, I have a three-day weekend.

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.760
I won't see everyone again till next week.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.690
The person you are calling
cannot come to the phone.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:39.490
Please leave a message after the tone.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.740
I guess she went out.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.830
I was hoping to apologize for calling her this morning, too.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.210
One taiyaki, please.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:10.310
There's always been someone around, so I was never really alone like this.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.230
It feels kinda weird.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.570
What's with the long face?

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.240
That's not like you at all.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:22.740
Noa?

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.700
I've never gone grocery shopping before.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.410
I didn't realize the bags would be so heavy.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.660
Give a girl a hand.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.710
You sure have a lot of girl friends now.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.170
Quit gawking. Get inside already!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.550
Wh-Why are you at my house?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.130
I'm not telling you, Casanova.

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:44.970
What?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.300
What took you so long?

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:48.970
Stop taking detours on your way home!

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.890
What?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.520
O-Okay...

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.350
I was against this.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:57.860
But, like, it wouldn't be fair if
only Aoi got to come here, right?

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:04.610
And I wanted all the details
on what happened today.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:09.580
You're a train nerd through
and through, huh, Takayama?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.370
Iwaizumi, was that supposed
to be a compliment?

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.910
It wasn't?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.210
You guys have tomorrow off, right?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.790
That means we can talk all night.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.340
Yeah.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:24.510
Maybe now's a good time to set
the record straight on a few things.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.890
B-Bring it on!

